      "title": "proto: Use wmem_map for gpa_name_map",
      "message": "proto: Use wmem_map for gpa_name_map\n\nUse a wmem_map for gpa_name_map, because we can reserve an initial\nnumber of entries. GHashTable doesn't have that functionality, and\nthe large number of resizes up to 245760 or 491510 elements impose\na startup cost.\n\nNote that GHashTable is an open addressing / probing hash table,\nwhereas wmem_map is a chaining hash table.\n",
